if others do things differently, or are we Doing It Wrong if we don't bow down to your wisdom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just an opinion, not an authotarian decree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-27-2018, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:06:33-08:00","id":1189847,"title":"","content":"And yet you express it every time someone suggests something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:18:58-08:00","id":1189849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189110-verbena-factions?p=1189847#post1189847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you express it every time someone suggests something different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only tell you what I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T08:15:47-08:00","id":1189868,"title":"","content":"And you've done so. Repeating it doesn't add anything to the topic, and borders on threadcrapping. Remember, the purpose of this thread is to explore alternatives to the official Verbena factions, not to argue whether or not there <i>should</i> be alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-27-2018, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T17:09:36-08:00","id":1190068,"title":"","content":"Maybe another way to look at Verbena factions are through a more meta look at the predecessors and successors of Mage: the Ascension. <br /> <br /> <b>Ars Magica</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>House Diedne</i> <a href=\"http://www.redcap.org/page/House_Diedne\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.redcap.org/page/House_Diedne</a> was a house of druids that joined the Order of Hermes until Tremere - not yet having succumbed to vampirism - accused them of committing human sacrifice and convinced the Quaesitors to rally the entire Order against them in 1011 AD. Most of them were killed in the war, but their leaders escaped and were not found. They may have hidden as members of the oft overlooked House Ex Miscellanea. <br /> <br /> <i>House Bjornaer</i> <a href=\"http://www.redcap.org/page/House_Bjornaer\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.redcap.org/page/House_Bjornaer</a> was another House of Hermes that originated as a nature revering religion or cult. They focused on shapeshifting into beasts that had personal and religious significance. <br /> <br /> By 1466, when the Council of Nine was established, members of the two above pagan houses left the Order of Hermes and joined the Verbenae. They have kept their traditions and practices alive ever since. <br /> <br /> <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Valdaermen </i><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Valdaermen\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Valdaermen</a> were a fellowship of norse rune-crafters. Their magic was often considered woman's magic, but that didn't stop Odin himself from sacrificing himself to himself in order to learn the powerful secrets of the runes. His followers - men and women - follow his example. In the official canon, the Vaeldermen split during the grand convocation between the Verbenae, the Chakravanti, and the Dreamspeakers. In modern times, their cultural descendents who worship Loki form the Hagalaz faction of the Cult of Ecstasy. <br /> <br /> The Old Faith fellowship contains several historical pagan groups that could persist as modern factions, and there's also a reference to a group called the <i>Aeduna</i> that moved through several pagan religions and claimed to have inspired other groups, such as the Cult of Ecstasy, the Dreamspeakers, and the Verbena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T18:57:11-08:00","id":1190094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189110-verbena-factions?p=1190068#post1190068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe another way to look at Verbena factions are through a more meta look at the predecessors and successors of Mage: the Ascension.<br /> <br /> <b>Ars Magica</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>House Diedne</i> <a href=\"http://www.redcap.org/page/House_Diedne\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.redcap.org/page/House_Diedne</a> was a house of druids that joined the Order of Hermes until Tremere - not yet having succumbed to vampirism - accused them of committing human sacrifice and convinced the Quaesitors to rally the entire Order against them in 1011 AD. Most of them were killed in the war, but their leaders escaped and were not found. They may have hidden as members of the oft overlooked House Ex Miscellanea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've long believed that the Diedne were framed by House Tremere's leadership in order to divert attention from their vampire project. (Their leadership allegedly may have escaped to Arcadia, and that thread is explored in Guide to the Traditions IIRC.) <br /> <br /> The Wild Heart faction in my post are meant to be the group that Bjornaer (derived from what I've read about them in Ars Magica books) initially came from when the Order of Hermes was formed, and to which a number of them returned at the Grand Convocation, with a minority staying in Ex Misc. At least that's what I've always taken to have happened. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:06:01-08:00","id":1190098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189110-verbena-factions?p=1190094#post1190094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've long believed that the Diedne were framed by House Tremere's leadership in order to divert attention from their vampire project. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this was explicitly stated somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T20:35:25-08:00","id":1190118,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Tremere turned against the Diedne specifically to divert from their vampire project. I don't know if said vampire project was going on at the time, or if it was in stages of development enough that it would need distracting from. House Tremere had MANY projects running around that time, working on alternative ways to prolong their lives. Hell, vampirism itself wasn't really the goal, but an unintended effect of a half-successful attempt at implementation. (Goratrix may have known it would happen, and Tremere himself may have as well, but most of the House thought the project would leave them...less undead).<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Tremere made accusations against Diedne simply for <i>general</i> political advantage. Politicking was the House founder's overriding preoccupation. He probably figured he could garner his House (and himself) a better position by inciting a war with a House that was already distrusted and insular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}